        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Miles Kane, Carl Barât, Pete Doherty\n- Organizations: The Libertines, The Last Shadow Puppets\n- Products: \"Don't Forget Who You Are\" (song), Don't Forget Who You Are (album), Anthems for Doomed Youth\n- Places: London, United Kingdom\n- Topics: English musicians, rock bands, garage rock\n\nFacts:\n- The Libertines were formed in London in 1997 by frontmen Carl Barât and Pete Doherty.\n- Miles Peter Kane was born on 17 March 1986 and is an English musician.\n- Miles Kane is best known as a solo artist and as the co-frontman of The Last Shadow Puppets.\n- Miles Kane released the song \"Don't Forget Who You Are\" from his second studio album of the same name as a digital download in the United Kingdom on 3 June 2013.\n- The Libertines are an English rock band.\n- Anthems for Doomed Youth is the third studio album by the English garage rock band The Libertines, released on 11 September 2015.",
